From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:01:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-akita: Give the main PMIC
 its interrupt

Without an interrupt the S2MPG14 driver supplies its rails but none of
the PMIC's events reach the host, so rtc0 has no wake alarm on the
Pixel 8a. The stock phone's s2mpg14mfd node has the same interrupt as
the Pixel 8 Pro's (interrupts = <0 0x4a 4 0>, GIC SPI 74, with
s2mpg14,wakeup enabled), and its /proc/interrupts shows rtc-alarm0 on
it. So this takes zuma-husky's three lines as they are: the interrupt,
latched by the VGPIO2AP sysreg, and wakeup-source.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
index e0a73f91c..039eadf76 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -167,6 +167,9 @@ cont_splash_mem: splash@fac00000 {
 &acpm_ipc {
 	pmic-1 {
 		compatible = "samsung,s2mpg14-pmic";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 74 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		google,vgpio2ap-sysreg = <&sysreg_vgpio2ap>;
+		wakeup-source;
 
 		regulators {
 			touch_avdd: ldo4m {
